<Base title="Getting there" description="How to get to Straussi Festival 2027 at the Straußäcker student residences in Stuttgart.">
  {/* English version of pages/anfahrt.astro. Keep both in sync. */}
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Getting there</h1>
    <p>The festival takes place on the grounds of the Straußäcker 1, 2 and 3 student residences in Stuttgart.</p>
    <h2>Address</h2>
    <p>Universitätsstraße 94<br />70569 Stuttgart<br />Germany</p>
    <Karte />
    <KalenderButton />
    <h2>By public transport</h2>
    <p>The best way to get here is by public transport.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>S-Bahn (suburban train):</strong> lines S1, S2 and S3 to the stop Universität, then about a 5-minute walk to the festival site.</li>
      <li><strong>Bus to Universität:</strong> lines 82, 84, 91, 92, X74, 747, 748 and X60 (right at the S-Bahn station).</li>
      <li><strong>Bus to Schranne:</strong> the closest stop, about a 2-minute walk away. Lines 82, 84, 91, 92, 747, 748, N1 and X74.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>By car</h2>
    <p>Only limited parking is available on Pfaffenwaldring near Stuttgart Media University (HdM) and the University of Stuttgart. Because space is limited, we strongly recommend coming by S-Bahn or bus.</p>
    {/* TODO: section "By bike" (bike parking, if available), once known. Hidden until then. */}
    <h2>Accommodation</h2>
    <p>There is no camping on site. There are hotels, hostels and Airbnb accommodation around Vaihingen and Stuttgart.</p>
    <h2>Site plan</h2>
    <p>The site plan will be available on site during the festival weekend.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
